There are a few things that are on my "wish list" that I didn't see
mentioned.  For brevity's sake, I'll go through the early-to-mid game
things I like to get.

1) Magic Resistance
2a) Reflection
2b) Poison Resistance

There are multiple ways to get all of these.  I ususally make Magic
Resistance my #1 priority from the start of the game.  How exactly I go
about getting all three depends highly on the game situation at the
time of the wish

4) a blessed greased rustproof +2 athame (usually not named Magicbane).

6 NAO ascentions (to date) had an athame in  main inventory.  Only once
was it Magicbane, and that was a gehennom bones pile pick-up.  *four*
of those were wished for.  The ability to liberally spam Elbereth from
on side of the dungeon to the other makes the game so much less
stressful.

5) a bag of holding

Only worthwhile *after* completing sokoban, and then only if it's the
reflection variant.

After those five, it's pretty much specific needs and remedies.  I
generally don't wish for non CoMR/foo-DSM armour (it just feels
wasteful).  Examples of some of the more "unconventional" wishes I've
made:

blessed unicorn horn (hadn't seen one yet)
blessed rustproof +2 Sunsword (style game)
two tins of fire giant meat (followed seconds later by two tins of red
dragon meat)

Barring something I want/need "right now" my default wish is usually a
blessed magic marker.

I disagree with your weapon recommendations, mainly because artifact
wishing is (often) wasteful.

> My recommendations for the first weapon wish.
> 1) Archeologist - Grayswandir

Only worthwhile for a neutral Arc.  Lawful can get Excalibur without
much difficulty and Grayswandir through sacrifice.

> 2) Barbarian - Grayswandir/ArtifactLongSword

Only worthwhile for a neutral Barb.  Chaotics can get Stormbringer

> 3) Caveman - Grayswandir

Meh, I don't really have an opinion here, yet.

> 4) Healer - Grayswandir

Upgrading from the Staff of Aesculapius to Grayswandir is about as
helpful as wishing for "nothing" in the late game.  Pre-quest, an elven
short sword and an athame is usually more than enough offense.

> 5) Knight - ArtifactLongSword/Grayswandir

Grayswandir + Elven Broadsword == Dances with Riders

> 6) Monk - Gauntlets of Power (Robe will allow casting of spells)

Spellbook of Magic Missile or Helm of Brilliance would be higher on my
list.

> 7) Priest - Grayswandir

Meh.  My only priest ascension went the almost entire game with my
starting mace and a glaive I'd picked up in the first room of Dlvl.1
... I didn't really miss not having an artifact weapon.

> 8) Ranger - Gauntlets of Power (upto four thrown daggers are deadly).

Poisoned +7 arrows do stupid amounts of damage and a stack of 200
weighs as much as 20 daggers.  With maxed out luck that's more than
enough for the endgame.

> 9) Rogue - Gauntlets of Power (4 daggers with backstab is even more
> so).

Only for orcish rogues, and then only with reservations.  I'd take an
athame first (or a tooled horn/leather drum)

> 10) Samurai - ArtifactLongSword

+7 Snickersnee and a +7 katana at maxed skill / strength averages over
40 points of damage per hit.  Why bother?

> 11) Tourist - Gauntlets of Power for expert thrown daggers/Grayswandir.

With maxed strength, GoP are a lose not a win for any non-Valkyre
human.

> 12) Valkyrie - ArtifactLongSword

Only for a neutral Valk.  Lawfuls can usually get Excalibur with ease.

> 13) Wizard - Spellbook of Magic Missile/Gauntlets of power.

Magic Marker.  Almost any other non-big-five wish is wasteful here.



